  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\lVert f(b)-f(a)\\rVert\\le C\\,|b-a| whenever \\lVert f'(t)\\rVert\\le C on the interval, with Banach-space Frechet-derivative analogues.",
    "plain": "Backfill the vector-valued mean-value inequality metadata: the classical equality becomes a norm bound, with Lipschitz consequences, ODE difference estimates, and Banach-space generalizations.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Vector-valued functions do not generally satisfy the scalar MVT equality, so the inequality is the right reusable theorem.",
      "Derivative bounds become Lipschitz and displacement estimates, which are central in analysis and ODE theory.",
      "The Banach-space version packages the same principle for Frechet derivatives."
    ]
  },
